{
  "id": "fluency-l7-power-rule",
  "lesson": "l7-power-rule",
  "title": "Fluency: the power rule",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "polynomial",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "differentiate a polynomial term by term",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "d": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "a3": "3*a", "b2": "2*b" },
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f({v}) = {poly(v; a, b, c, d)}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{poly(v; a3, b2, c)}", "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "power-not-lowered", "tex": "{poly(v; a3, b2, c, 0)}", "line": "You brought each power down but did not lower it by one." },
        { "id": "constant-kept", "tex": "{poly(v; a3, b2, c + d)}", "line": "You kept the constant {d}, but a constant on its own has slope 0." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Bring each power down and lower it by one: ${a:c}{v}^3$ gives ${a3}{v}^2$ and ${b:c}{v}^2$ gives ${b2}{v}$.",
        "The term in ${v}$ gives {c} and the constant {d} gives 0.",
        "So $f'({v}) = {poly(v; a3, b2, c)}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negative-power",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "differentiate a power of x on the bottom",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [1, 9] },
        "s": { "pick": [1, -1] },
        "n": { "int": [2, 6] }
      },
      "let": { "k": "-n*a*s", "e": "-n-1", "sa": "s*a" },
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x) = {s:c}\\dfrac{{{a}}}{{x^{{{n}}}}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{k}x^{{{e}}}", "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "bottom-differentiated", "tex": "\\frac{{{sa}}}{{{n}}}x^{{{1-n}}}", "line": "You differentiated the bottom in place. Write the term as ${sa:c}x^{{{-n}}}$ first." },
        { "id": "power-raised", "tex": "{k}x^{{{1-n}}}", "line": "You raised the power by one. The power rule lowers it, so $-{n}$ becomes ${e}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Write it as a power: $f(x) = {sa:c}x^{{{-n}}}$.",
        "Bring the power down and lower it by one: $f'(x) = {sa} \\times {-n:()} \\, x^{{{e}}} = {k}x^{{{e}}}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fractional-power",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "differentiate a fractional power",
      "vars": {
        "q": { "pick": [2, 3] },
        "p": { "int": [-5, 7], "not": [0] },
        "m": { "int": [1, 5] },
        "s": { "pick": [1, -1] }
      },
      "let": { "k": "s*m*q", "c": "s*m*p", "e": "(p - q)/q", "eu": "(p + q)/q" },
      "where": ["p % q != 0"],
      "prompt": "Differentiate $f(x) = {k}x^{{{p/q:frac}}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{c:c}x^{{{e:frac}}}", "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "power-raised", "tex": "{c:c}x^{{{eu:frac}}}", "line": "You raised the power by one. The power rule lowers it by one." },
        { "id": "power-not-brought-down", "tex": "{k}x^{{{e:frac}}}", "line": "You lowered the power but did not multiply by it." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Bring the power ${p/q:frac}$ down: ${k}$ times it is ${c}$.",
        "Lower the power by one: ${p/q:frac} - 1 = {e:frac}$.",
        "So $f'(x) = {c:c}x^{{{e:frac}}}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slope-at-a-point",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "find the slope of a polynomial at a point",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-3, 3], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-9, 9] },
        "d": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "k": { "int": [-3, 3], "not": [0, 1] }
      },
      "let": {
        "a3": "3*a", "b2": "2*b",
        "r": "3*a*k^2 + 2*b*k + c",
        "fk": "a*k^3 + b*k^2 + c*k + d",
        "np": "3*a*k^3 + 2*b*k^2 + c*k"
      },
      "where": ["fk != r", "np != r", "fk != np"],
      "prompt": "Take $f(x) = {poly(x; a, b, c, d)}$. Work out $f'({k})$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{r}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "value-not-slope", "value": "{fk}", "line": "That is $f({k})$, the height. Differentiate first, then put $x = {k}$ in." },
        { "id": "power-not-lowered", "value": "{np}", "line": "You brought each power down but did not lower it by one." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$f'(x) = {poly(x; a3, b2, c)}$.",
        "Put $x = {k}$ in: $f'({k}) = {r}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
